Recommends: projectm
Suggests: python3-openrgb, openrgb, python3-numpy
Description: KDE Plasma controller for the projectM MilkDrop visualiser
 MilkDropper sits in the system tray and manages the projectM music visualiser
 in three modes: as a live Plasma wallpaper rendered behind desktop icons, as a
 standalone projectMSDL window, or off.
 .
 The wallpaper mode is a native Qt Quick renderer that drives libprojectM
 directly and captures system audio through PipeWire/PulseAudio. The tray menu
 exposes per-source audio routing and preset controls (next, previous, random,
 lock).
 .
 Desktop mode requires Plasma's Qt Quick scene graph to run on OpenGL; see
 /usr/share/doc/milkdropper/README.Debian for how to enable it.

Package: milkdropper-standalone
Architecture: any
Conflicts: milkdropper, libprojectm4-gles
Replaces: milkdropper, libprojectm4-gles
Provides: milkdropper
Depends: ${shlibs:Depends},
         ${misc:Depends},
         python3,
         python3-pyqt6,
         plasma-workspace,
         libpulse0,
         pulseaudio-utils
Recommends: projectm
Suggests: python3-openrgb, openrgb, python3-numpy
Description: KDE Plasma controller for projectM (self-contained build)
 Identical to the milkdropper package, but ships its own copy of the OpenGL ES
 build of libprojectM 4 instead of depending on libprojectm4-gles.
 .
 Use this variant when installing a single .deb by hand on a system that has no
 access to the libprojectm4-gles package.
